WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.310
- All right ya'll we're back,

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.920
and I'm hanging with Paula
Pell, Sara Bareilles,

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.300
Busy Phillipps, and
Renee Elise Goldsberry.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.605
Give it up!

00:00:07.605 --> 00:00:08.670
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.910
Together they play a girl
group in the new show

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.960
Girls5eva on peacock.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.120
So it's time to find
out y'all who you'd be

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.500
in the girl group in real life.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.730
So I'll give you one
question to each of you,

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.700
but then you all should answer
after that person answers.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.533
Get it?

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:27.650
I think you get, yeah, I
think you follow. (chuckles)

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.500
All right, here we go.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.460
Busy. Who in the group
trips walking out on stage?

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.728
- Well, our dear Paula Pell, and me,

00:00:36.728 --> 00:00:40.270
but Paula you just knocked over a

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.491
- You just knocked over
two stands on the way out.

00:00:42.491 --> 00:00:44.672
(laughing hysterically)

00:00:44.672 --> 00:00:46.580
- [Paula] I'm I'm, I'm
not a graceful person.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.150
I ride low, like fog.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.630
I just kind of fill in the spaces

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:53.787
and if something's in the
way it's going down, so.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.030
- She knows how to make an
entrance, that's what it is

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.900
- I ride low, like fog

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.730
- I'm very solid, I, I
hold my gravity very low.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.610
- Yeah. So wait I'm Sarah

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.405
who do you think is the most,
you know, most likely to trip?

00:01:09.405 --> 00:01:10.645
- Well, I don't know.

00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:14.200
I, I guess I would agree that, you know,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.180
I think we all have really
clumsy mo- know, I'm honest.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.700
It's popped in my mind.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.700
When, when Busy hit Renee in
the face with a salad bowl.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.537
- What?!

00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:26.565
- [Sara] Yes.

00:01:26.565 --> 00:01:28.410
- Wait what'd you do?

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.303
- Oh my god, I almost forgot.

00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:36.209
- Yeah, we were shooting
a scene in a closet

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.700
and there was a gag where
she was supposed to, you know

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.267
spill, toss the salad as it were.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.339
(audience laughing)

00:01:44.339 --> 00:01:46.580
And the next thing I
know, I was like, cut!

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.410
- Oh my gosh, okay, so then

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.023
- The shot of me talking
like this is still in it.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:57.950
- But the best part is
like Renee keeps asking us,

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.870
like you guys, is it bad? Is it bad?

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:03.170
And it's like, her lip is
like four times the size.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.205
And we're just like, no it's fine.

00:02:05.205 --> 00:02:06.130
- There all lying

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.460
- No, no just keep acting

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.230
- I walked in after the
whole thing happened

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.480
and it was a very weird energy on the set.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.030
Everyone was whispering.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.430
She got a giant bag of ice

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.220
on her face and Busy was
kind of pacing around.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.380
- See, this is what I imagined.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.555
Girl groups are like.

00:02:23.555 --> 00:02:25.210
(laughing)

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.250
- It was very funny.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.790
- I know you can't laugh until later,

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:28.990
but then you laugh hysterically.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:30.470
Like you've been holding it for a minute.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.580
Cause you wanted to laugh before.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.090
So Paula who in the group curses onstage?

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.980
- Well, I would say Busy and I

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.115
probably are the foulest
mouths of these four beauties.

00:02:42.115 --> 00:02:44.740
I was on, when we did wine country.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.190
When we went on the today show in

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.880
within 30 seconds, I said the S word.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.160
- Oh, they, they frowned upon that,

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.480
I've slipped before.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.030
- Yeah, I mean like immediately,

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.260
I think it was the first thing

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.980
I uttered and it was just one of those.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.157
Like somebody said
something amazing and I went

00:03:00.157 --> 00:03:00.990
(mouths the s word)

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:01.823
and I just said it.

00:03:01.823 --> 00:03:05.240
And everyone looked at
me like I had, you know

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.073
- [Kelly] killed someone?

00:03:06.073 --> 00:03:07.204
- Pooped in their purse.

00:03:07.204 --> 00:03:08.884
(audience laughing)

00:03:08.884 --> 00:03:10.740
And I was like, I am very sorry.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.870
I guess I can't say that on
the Today show in the mornings

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.020
and my mother was watching.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:17.840
So, but I think Busy and I are both pretty

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.830
unfiltered when it comes
to vocabulary like that

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:21.860
- I, I'm unfiltered too.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:24.230
But do y'all feel like
you, well, first of all

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:26.780
I feel like I became unfiltered
when I was a waitress

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.500
because there were four letter words.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.600
We're the only ones that felt good saying,

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.840
but I don't ever say it really in anger.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.980
Mine's like, I just come in conversation.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:36.813
I'm like

00:03:36.813 --> 00:03:39.050
- I always, I usually say it either in

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.380
in joy or every so often,

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.164
if I'm really frustrated
about something, I'll

00:03:43.164 --> 00:03:46.600
I'll use a good juicy word,
but a lot of times you just,

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.140
it's just becomes part of your vernacular

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.140
of just of joyful telling
a story or whatever.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.750
- I get it. I get it. Busy you too,

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.170
You got a potty mouth?

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.870
- Yeah, same

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.970
You know, it's hard for me.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.913
I just enjoy saying the words.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:04.953
- I do too.

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:06.790
My mother can't stand the F word.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.920
I know whatever, but it's sorry mom.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:13.130
It's literally one of my
favorite words, you know?

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:14.308
And anyway, I think

00:04:14.308 --> 00:04:17.500
(indistinct)

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.580
- [Kelly] You come from
a long line of what?

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.500
- I come from a long
line of women that curse.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.630
And I'm kind of proud of that.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.463
I'm kind of proud of it.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.030
I think there's something beautiful

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.490
about a woman that's that doesn't like

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.460
feel like she has to censor her emotion

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.900
and how it comes out of her mouth.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.440
I think that's very ladylike.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.100
- I hope my mom, we're
going to keep this in.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.220
So she hears that she, yeah

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.380
she didn't appreciate it as much as us.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.293
So Renee, who's the leader of the group?

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.240
- Well, in terms of the gosh,
you know, there's a really

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.740
we're all very strong, but there's one

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:52.190
of us who is the ringleader,
especially when it comes

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.610
to doing something important
or amazing, amazing

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:56.640
or celebrating each other.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.670
And that is Busy Phillips.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:02.580
She is always like, you
know, 20 steps ahead.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.410
She just like, we shot the show.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:05.930
I've got me, we hit Christmas.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.410
We hit, you know, new year's.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.950
We hit a lot of birthdays and you know

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.670
way before anybody can think about it.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:14.950
This girl has an idea to make some merch.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:18.400
We have Girls5eva everything, just

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.950
because she's going to find
a way to give a present.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.340
Would, that's been thought of.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.480
Celebrate somebody amazing,

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.160
to everybody in the cast
and crew, you know, and

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.600
the worst part is she always
makes sure we all want to go

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.930
in on it for her, but she never
takes our money afterwards.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.200
- No, we still don't know her Venmo.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.350
So if anyone knows her Venmo

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.730
In, in the viewing audience

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.560
please send it to us because we,

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.500
- Listen Paula I get requests
every day from random people,

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.147
so I feel like you can probably find it.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.820
(audience laughing)

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.120
- I'll always take the lead.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.840
I'll always pick the gifts.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.140
That's, I love doing it.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:54.973
- I do too.

00:05:54.973 --> 00:05:57.020
I think I'm that person
in my group. I love it.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.560
I think mine comes from like,
I always felt bad when like

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:02.220
in childhood, like when
anybody felt left out

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.770
so I never wanted anybody
to not be included.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:05.860
So I like try and go.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.450
Now my friends will say, I
go way too, above and beyond.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:10.770
And then I stress myself out doing it,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.240
as I'm learning in therapy.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.430
But, but yeah, but I think

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.780
but I think it's a really,
it's a nice thing though.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:18.320
You're trying to make everybody feel

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.110
like welcome and a part of something.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:22.650
And I love being a part of a team so.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:23.900
Well we are out of time right now.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.670
Thank you so much, ladies.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.120
You can watch all episodes

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.353
of Girls5eva on peacock starting tomorrow.

